Body:
Adding two data points that extend @munir-weave's timing analysis and sharpen the failure signature for @holny's fix (repro details below, raw JSON-RPC against `opencode acp`, no third-party client — consistent with the snapshot-timing finding: the catalog the ACP layer serves looks like a pre-config-merge snapshot, which is why only bare upstream ids and the generic effort ladder appear).

**1. Set-accepts / prompt-rejects split.** `session/set_config_option` with a *generic* effort value (`high` from the advertised `none/minimal/low/medium/high/default` ladder) is accepted and stored on the session — then the prompt-time resolver rejects the same ref against the config-merged catalog:

```text
→ set_config_option { configId: "model",  value: "ollama-cloud/deepseek-v4.1-flash" }   ← ok
→ set_config_option { configId: "effort", value: "high" }                               ← ok
→ prompt { ... }
← -32603 "Internal error: Variant unavailable for ollama-cloud/deepseek-v4.1-flash: high"
   data: { "service": "session", "errorName": "provider.no-route" }
```

So a host that picks only from advertised options — protocol-correct behavior — still produces a session that fails at first prompt, surfaced as a generic `provider.no-route` error rather than invalid-params. Same root as #50378. A regression test for the fix should assert not only that `configOptions` contains the config-defined entries, but that a set-then-prompt using advertised values succeeds.

**2. A verified workaround** (no fix required): make the config coincide with what the pre-merge snapshot advertises — bare upstream model ids, variant ids renamed to the generic ladder, same `reasoningEffort` values:

```jsonc
{
  "providers": {
    "ollama-cloud": {
      "models": {
        // was "deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud" with variants thinking/low-effort/max-effort
        "deepseek-v4.1-flash": {
          "limit": { "context": 1000000, "output": 32768 },
          "variants": [
            { "id": "low",  "settings": { "reasoningEffort": "low" } },
            { "id": "high", "settings": { "reasoningEffort": "high" } },
            { "id": "max",  "settings": { "reasoningEffort": "max" } }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Verified end-to-end on 2.0.16: after this change, sessions selected entirely from advertised options resolve and prompt.

Environment: opencode 2.0.16, macOS 15 arm64 (official bun binary), config-only OpenAI-compatible providers (`aisdk:@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`, suffixed ids like `deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud`, custom variant names `thinking`/`low-effort`/`max-effort` — all resolvable in the TUI). The original failure was observed through an ACP desktop host as `provider.no-route` cards at first prompt.
